    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The bank is recovered. The last two recovery checks in a row ran clean, and the final look was at 56 s.",
      "background": "The scheduler changed payments max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1. A reconciliation session held a write lock on the ledger for 11.5 s, and the gateway went down. Primary fraud screening then timed out on every call from payments, with p95 at 1027 ms against a 1.0 s timeout.",
      "assessment": "The incident commander did each of these itself, and each one completed. It ended the reconciliation session holding the ledger lock, reverted payments max_transfer_minor from 1 to 1000000, and restarted the gateway. It then failed screening over to screening-standby, whose last event was a start on release 4.1, which cleared the 91% failure rate at payments and gateway.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why primary fraud screening became slow before failing back from standby, and find out why the scheduler set max_transfer_minor to 1. Operations should check that the reconciliation batch, which was ended mid-run, is rerun and completes. They should also review payments that failed or were blocked during the incident."
    },
